      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>A little about me</h2>
        <p>I’m a Mathematics undergraduate at National Cheng Kung University. Mathematics gives me a way to think carefully about problems; programming lets me try those ideas out. Research is one part of my life, alongside teaching, community activities, and the things I’m still curious enough to try.</p>
        <p>My personal motto is simple: <strong>“Trying new things, learning as I go.”</strong> I enjoy stepping into unfamiliar areas, asking questions, and improving through practice. I don’t expect every experiment to work the first time; I value what the process teaches me.</p>
      </section>
